Subject: [PATCH] kcm_wifi_mobile: Toggle Wi-Fi only on user click

The Wi-Fi switch called handler.enableWireless() from onCheckedChanged and
then re-created the checked binding inside the same handler. The re-bind
changes checked back to the (not yet updated) NetworkManager state, which
fires onCheckedChanged again and sends the opposite value; when
NetworkManager answers, the binding changes checked once more. One tap
therefore starts an endless on/off ping-pong of WirelessEnabled writes
(hundreds per minute), the switch ends up stuck off and the radio flaps.

React to the click only, as the switch did before: onClicked is not
emitted for programmatic changes of checked.

---
--- a/kcms/kcm_wifi_mobile/ui/main.qml	2026-11-10 08:29:30.000000000 +0100
+++ b/kcms/kcm_wifi_mobile/ui/main.qml	2026-11-14 12:31:28.496014851 +0100
@@ -86,7 +86,7 @@
                 id: wifiSwitch
                 text: i18n("Wi-Fi")
                 checked: enabledConnections.wirelessEnabled
-                onCheckedChanged: {
+                onClicked: {
                     handler.enableWireless(checked);
                     checked = Qt.binding(() => enabledConnections.wirelessEnabled);
                 }
